      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142737",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a population where some individuals have a particular characteristic.\nFind a lower bound for sample size $n$ required to ensure that the margin of error for the $95%$ confidence interval for the population proportion of individuals with the characteristic is at most $0.04$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.96) = 0.025$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
