      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143229",
      ":question/problem": "During an election year, the number of individuals supporting a particular candidate has grown significantly. Find a lower bound for sample size $n$ needed to ensure that the margin of error of the $99%$ confidence interval for the population proportion of individuals supporting that candidate is at most $0.04$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 2.576) = 0.005$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
